                >
                    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 bg-[#FF4500] text-white font-black text-xs uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-2 rounded-bl-xl">
                        ★ Our Verdict
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-white mt-0 mb-6 border-none">Which Polymeric Sand Alternative Is Best?</h2>
                    <div class="space-y-6 text-gray-300">
                        <p>
                            <strong class="text-white">Best Overall Alternative: Paver Joint Sealer + Regular Sand.</strong> This combination gives you bonded, weed-proof, insect-proof joints with zero hazing risk and the added benefit of surface sealing — all for roughly the same cost as polymeric sand. It is the smartest upgrade path for anyone who has been burned by polymeric sand hazing or frustrated by its fussy installation requirements.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            <strong class="text-white">Best Budget Alternative: Stone Dust.</strong> At a fraction of the cost of any polymer-based product, stone dust compacts more tightly than regular sand, provides moderate weed resistance, and offers a natural appearance that works beautifully with stone and rustic paver designs. It is the best value option for large projects and budget-conscious homeowners.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            <strong class="text-white">Best Eco-Friendly Alternative: EnviroSAND.</strong> For homeowners who want hardening performance similar to polymeric sand without introducing synthetic plastics into their yard's ecosystem, EnviroSAND is the clear winner. Its plant-based binder and organic weed inhibitor deliver genuine performance through an entirely natural mechanism.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-lg border-t border-gray-700 pt-6 mt-6">
                            <strong class="text-[#38BDF8]">Bottom Line:</strong> Polymeric sand is still the single best all-around paver jointing product for most residential projects. But if cost, environmental impact, installation difficulty, or hazing risk are deal-breakers for you, <strong class="text-white">each of these five alternatives solves a specific problem that polymeric sand does not</strong>. Choose based on your top priority, and you will get a result that serves your project better than defaulting to polymeric sand in a situation where it is not ideal.
                        </p>
